{"Critical bug: `start` and `end` are both calculated using the same value (`slotStartTime`). The `end` calculation should use `slotEndTime` instead, causing the working hours check to compare the slot start time against both the startTime and endTime boundaries, which will incorrectly reject valid slots.": 0.9867045879364014, "Condition uses strict equality (`===`) to compare two Dayjs objects, which will always return `false` since they are different object instances. Should use `.isSame()` instead. This bug could allow bookings when the host marked themselves as unavailable all day.": 0.9571120738983154, "The tRPC router layer is becoming an overgrown orchestrator managing multiple scheduling concerns (workingHours, dateOverrides, organizerTimeZone). Consider extracting a ScheduleContext object to group related concerns.": 0.013274543918669224, "Timezone offset calculations are duplicated across the router layer (checkIfIsAvailable) and slots layer (getSlots), creating a maintenance liability where logic drift could occur silently. Should consolidate into a shared utility function.": 0.11334341019392014, "Override and timezone semantics are scattered across multiple pieces of context (organizerTimeZone, invitee timezone, UTC offsets). The complex temporal logic lacks encapsulation\u2014should extract a dedicated helper like resolveActiveOverridesForDay() to centralize this complexity.": 0.017842646688222885, "Integration test coverage exists but lacks focused unit tests for DST boundaries and organizer-vs-invitee day crossovers, leaving edge cases unvalidated.": 0.2144702523946762}